{
  "_readme": ["Curated. The one data owner for item materials and the Sieg's Guide durability breakdown; read by utils/class_func/item_materials.py and gated by scripts/gates/validate_item_materials.py.", "weapon_base / shield_base / armor_base / enhancement and the first ten substances are transcribed from the Sieg's Guide 'Combat References' doc (Equipment Hardness/Hitpoints + Substance Chart). coldIron, alchemicalSilver and darkwood are not on that chart; their rows are the printed PF1e values.", "Material ids are the pf1 system's own (pf1.registry.materials), so the Foundry module can write them straight into system.material.", "weapons: every weapons_data.json name appears in exactly one group. `row` is the hardness-table row, `material` the substance the durability breakdown adds, `metal_parts` marks a wooden-hafted weapon whose head can still be a special metal. armor / shields: the same idea for armor.json.", "special_materials.price, per slot: `flat` gp; `per_pound` gp x the item's listed weight; `by_category` keyed by weapon category or armor section; `cost_multiplier` x the item's own cost; `enchant_surcharge` gp owed only if the item is also enchanted."],
